From 7d01dfc52604d08058f68137b63507ccd452e729 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 09:42:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix multi-page printed invoice pagination and layout

The printed invoice relied on the browser to split one long page. With @page margin 0
(needed to hide Chrome's own date/URL header) the later pages had no margin, no header
and no page numbers, and the payment status could be pushed onto page 2 alone, away
from the totals.

Just before printing, the invoice is now laid out on explicit paper-sized pages
(java script/invoice-print.js), measured in the real browser:

- Financial summary (subtotal, discount, tax, total, paid, remaining and the payment
  status) is one block that is never split; it stays under the products when it fits.
- Product rows flow across pages, one row per entry, with the column headings repeated.
- Payment history and delivery history flow independently; heading + first entry stay
  together, later pages repeat the heading as "(continued)".
- Pages 2+ get a compact "INVOICE - CONTINUED" header (company, number, date, customer).
- Every page has consistent margins and a "Page X of N" footer; N is the real count.
- The thank-you message follows the last section and only moves when it does not fit.
- If laying out the pages fails, the browser prints the preview as before.

Invoice data, calculations, screen preview and the purchase / collection documents are
unchanged. Adds layout unit tests, markup tests and a real-browser PDF check.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
